1
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:58,410
Easy, boy.

2
00:03:12,250 --> 00:03:14,630
What do you expect? They're savages.

3
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:17,000
One lot steals a goat from another lot,

4
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,270
before you know it they're ripping each other to pieces.

5
00:03:19,270 --> 00:03:21,870
I've never seen wildlings do a thing like this.

6
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:24,370
I never seen a thing like this, not ever in my life.

7
00:03:25,530 --> 00:03:28,390
- How close did you get? - Close as any man would.

8
00:03:28,390 --> 00:03:30,130
We should head back to the wall.

9
00:03:32,610 --> 00:03:34,200
Do the dead frighten you?

10
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:36,570
Our orders were to track the wildlings.

11
00:03:36,570 --> 00:03:39,840
We tracked them. They won't trouble us no more.

12
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:42,350
You don't think he'll ask us how they died?

13
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:46,130
Get back on your horse.

14
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,080
Whatever did it to them could do it to us.

15
00:03:53,560 --> 00:03:55,220
They even killed the children.

16
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:57,810
It's a good thing we're not children.

17
00:03:59,490 --> 00:04:02,160
You want to run away south, run away.

18
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,340
Of course they will behead you as a deserter,

19
00:04:05,510 --> 00:04:07,840
if I don't catch you first.

20
00:04:09,850 --> 00:04:11,960
Get back on your horse.

21
00:04:12,430 --> 00:04:14,050
I won't say it again.

22
00:04:45,730 --> 00:04:48,570
Your dead men seem to have moved camp.

23
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:50,240
They were here.

24
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:55,380
See where they went.

25
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:43,510
What is it?

26
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:46,720
It's...

27
00:09:49,530 --> 00:09:51,850
Go on, father's watching.

28
00:09:54,660 --> 00:09:55,880
And your mother.

29
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:05,940
Fine work as always. Well done.

30
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:07,100
Thank you.

31
00:10:07,410 --> 00:10:11,330
I love the detail that you've managed to get in these corners.

32
00:10:11,330 --> 00:10:12,670
Quite beautiful.

33
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,430
The stitching...

34
00:10:36,680 --> 00:10:39,420
And which one of you was a marksman at 10?

35
00:10:40,290 --> 00:10:41,860
Keep practicing, Bran.

36
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:45,020
Go on.

37
00:10:46,430 --> 00:10:48,210
Don't think too much, Bran.

38
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:52,740
Relax your bow arm.

39
00:11:05,270 --> 00:11:06,900
Quick, Bran! Faster.

40
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,480
Lord Stark!

41
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:13,780
My lady.

42
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:16,700
A guardsman just rode in from the hills.

43
00:11:17,020 --> 00:11:19,360
They've captured a deserter from the Night's Watch.

44
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:25,340
Get the lads to saddle their horses.

45
00:11:25,450 --> 00:11:27,070
Do you have to?

46
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,250
He swore an oath, Cat.

47
00:11:29,580 --> 00:11:31,460
The law is law, my lady.

48
00:11:32,820 --> 00:11:34,520
Tell Bran he's coming too.

49
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:37,800
Ned.

50
00:11:38,150 --> 00:11:40,850
10 is too young to see such things.

51
00:11:40,850 --> 00:11:42,680
He won't be a boy forever.

52
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:46,190
And winter is coming.

53
00:12:05,590 --> 00:12:08,300
Good lad, go run back and get the rest.

54
00:12:13,760 --> 00:12:15,100
White walkers.

55
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:17,450
I saw the white walkers.

56
00:12:18,150 --> 00:12:19,550
White walkers.

57
00:12:20,330 --> 00:12:23,210
The white walkers, I saw them.

58
00:12:31,970 --> 00:12:33,600
I know I broke my oath.

59
00:12:34,660 --> 00:12:36,310
And I know I'm a deserter.

60
00:12:36,990 --> 00:12:39,470
I should have gone back to the wall and warned them, but...

61
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:42,410
I saw what I saw.

62
00:12:43,110 --> 00:12:44,820
I saw the white walkers.

63
00:12:46,940 --> 00:12:48,350
People need to know.

64
00:12:50,570 --> 00:12:52,420
If you can get word to my family...

65
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:54,710
Tell them I'm no coward.

66
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:56,610
Tell them I'm sorry.

67
00:13:13,870 --> 00:13:15,270
Forgive me, lord.

68
00:13:20,250 --> 00:13:23,620
In the name of Robert of the House Baratheon, the first of his name...

69
00:13:23,630 --> 00:13:24,730
Don't look away.

70
00:13:24,730 --> 00:13:26,190
...King of the Andals and the First Men...

71
00:13:26,190 --> 00:13:27,460
Father will know if you do.

72
00:13:27,460 --> 00:13:30,460
...Lord of the Seven Kingdoms and protector of the realm,

73
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:33,480
I, Eddard of the House Stark,

74
00:13:33,970 --> 00:13:36,710
Lord of Winterfell and warden of the north,

75
00:13:37,290 --> 00:13:38,940
sentence you to die.

76
00:13:53,750 --> 00:13:55,100
You did well.

77
00:14:23,690 --> 00:14:25,350
You understand why I did it?

78
00:14:25,410 --> 00:14:27,290
Jon said he was a deserter.

79
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:29,730
But do you understand why I had to kill him?

80
00:14:29,830 --> 00:14:31,510
"Our way is the old way"?

81
00:14:33,090 --> 00:14:36,970
The man who passes the sentence should swing the sword.

82
00:14:37,770 --> 00:14:39,800
Is it true he saw the white walkers?

83
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:45,510
The white walkers have been gone for thousands of years.

84
00:14:46,420 --> 00:14:47,870
So he was lying?

85
00:14:52,250 --> 00:14:54,570
A madman sees what he sees.

86
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:21,990
What is it?

87
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,450
Mountain lion?

88
00:15:27,990 --> 00:15:30,270
There are no mountain lions in these woods.

89
00:16:16,500 --> 00:16:17,770
It's a freak!

90
00:16:19,780 --> 00:16:21,300
It's a direwolf.

91
00:16:30,330 --> 00:16:31,910
Tough old beast.

92
00:16:34,690 --> 00:16:36,790
There are no direwolves south of the wall.

93
00:16:37,690 --> 00:16:39,280
Now there are five.

94
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:41,980
You want to hold it?

95
00:16:46,890 --> 00:16:48,350
Where will they go?

96
00:16:49,070 --> 00:16:50,220
Their mother's dead.

97
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:51,950
They don't belong down here.

98
00:16:52,140 --> 00:16:53,770
Better a quick death.

99
00:16:54,690 --> 00:16:55,980
They won't last without their mother.

100
00:16:55,980 --> 00:16:58,490
- Right. Give it here. - No!

101
00:16:58,490 --> 00:16:59,920
Put away your blade.

102
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:01,830
I take orders from your father, not you.

103
00:17:01,830 --> 00:17:04,950
- Please, father! - I'm sorry, Bran.

104
00:17:04,950 --> 00:17:06,230
Lord Stark?

105
00:17:07,810 --> 00:17:09,560
There are five pups...

106
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:12,630
One for each of the Stark children.

107
00:17:13,330 --> 00:17:15,600
The direwolf is the sigil of your house.

108
00:17:16,610 --> 00:17:18,010
They were meant to have them.

109
00:17:24,230 --> 00:17:26,140
You will train them yourselves.

110
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,050
You will feed them yourselves.

111
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:31,600
And if they die, you will bury them yourselves.

112
00:17:40,010 --> 00:17:41,340
What about you?

113
00:17:42,480 --> 00:17:43,970
I'm not a Stark.

114
00:17:44,820 --> 00:17:46,100
Get on.

115
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:57,970
What is it?

116
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:06,070
The runt of the litter... That one's yours, Snow.

117
00:19:05,700 --> 00:19:08,990
As your brother, I feel it's my duty to warn you:

118
00:19:10,070 --> 00:19:14,020
you worry too much. It's starting to show.

119
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:16,040
And you never worry about anything.

120
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:20,230
When we were seven and you jumped off the cliffs at Casterly Rock,

121
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:23,670
100-foot drop into the water,

122
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,910
and you were never afraid.

123
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:28,900
There was nothing to be afraid of until you told father.

124
00:19:28,940 --> 00:19:29,970
"We're Lannisters.

125
00:19:29,980 --> 00:19:32,320
Lannisters don't act like fools."

126
00:19:34,190 --> 00:19:36,340
What if Jon Arryn told someone?

127
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:38,030
But who would he tell?

128
00:19:39,100 --> 00:19:42,020
- My husband. - If he told the king, both our heads

129
00:19:42,020 --> 00:19:44,850
would be skewered on the city gates by now.

130
00:19:45,770 --> 00:19:49,220
Whatever Jon Arryn knew or didn't know, it died with him.

131
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,570
And Robert will choose a new Hand of the King...

132
00:19:51,570 --> 00:19:52,560
someone to do his job

133
00:19:52,560 --> 00:19:55,540
while he's off fucking boars and hunting whores...

134
00:19:55,540 --> 00:19:57,370
Or is it the other way around?

135
00:19:59,010 --> 00:20:01,200
And life will go on.

136
00:20:01,430 --> 00:20:03,460
You should be the Hand of the King.

137
00:20:04,450 --> 00:20:06,560
That's an honor I can do without.

138
00:20:06,560 --> 00:20:08,210
Their days are too long,

139
00:20:08,210 --> 00:20:10,550
their lives are too short.

140
00:20:49,470 --> 00:20:50,720
All these years

141
00:20:50,730 --> 00:20:52,660
and I still feel like an outsider

142
00:20:52,670 --> 00:20:54,160
when I come here.

143
00:20:55,870 --> 00:20:57,970
You have five northern children.

144
00:20:58,850 --> 00:21:00,530
You're not an outsider.

145
00:21:01,350 --> 00:21:03,550
I wonder if the old gods agree.

146
00:21:05,130 --> 00:21:07,180
It's your gods with all the rules.

147
00:21:13,470 --> 00:21:15,990
I am so sorry, my love.

148
00:21:16,870 --> 00:21:20,930
- Tell me. - There was a raven from King's Landing.

149
00:21:22,560 --> 00:21:24,700
Jon Arryn is dead.

150
00:21:25,230 --> 00:21:26,750
A fever took him.

151
00:21:30,050 --> 00:21:32,400
I know he was like a father to you.

152
00:21:34,920 --> 00:21:38,200
- Your sister, the boy? - They both have their health,

153
00:21:38,210 --> 00:21:39,750
gods be good.

154
00:21:50,450 --> 00:21:52,680
The raven brought more news...

155
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:56,380
The king rides for Winterfell...

156
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:58,630
with the queen

157
00:21:58,630 --> 00:22:00,520
and all the rest of them.

158
00:22:01,150 --> 00:22:03,270
If he's coming this far north,

159
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:07,170
there's only one thing he's after.

160
00:22:07,660 --> 00:22:10,470
You can always say no, Ned.

161
00:22:18,860 --> 00:22:22,490
We'll need plenty of candles for Lord Tyrion's chamber.

162
00:22:22,490 --> 00:22:24,750
I'm told he reads all night.

163
00:22:24,750 --> 00:22:26,640
I'm told he drinks all night.

164
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:29,780
How much could he possibly drink? A man of his...

165
00:22:29,780 --> 00:22:31,110
stature?

166
00:22:31,520 --> 00:22:34,340
We've brought up eight barrels of ale from the cellar.

167
00:22:34,540 --> 00:22:37,030
- Perhaps we'll find out. - In any case,

168
00:22:37,030 --> 00:22:38,580
candles.

169
00:22:43,830 --> 00:22:46,890
Why is your mother so dead set on us getting pretty for the King?

170
00:22:46,890 --> 00:22:48,350
It's for the Queen, I bet.

171
00:22:48,350 --> 00:22:50,010
I hear she's a sleek bit of mink.

172
00:22:50,010 --> 00:22:51,930
I hear the Prince is a right royal prick.

173
00:22:51,930 --> 00:22:53,740
Think of all those southern girls he gets to stab

174
00:22:53,740 --> 00:22:55,560
with his right royal prick.

175
00:22:57,470 --> 00:22:59,430
Go on, Tommy, shear him good.

176
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:02,360
He's never met a girl he likes better than his own hair.

177
00:23:40,110 --> 00:23:42,180
Gods, but they grow fast.

178
00:23:43,860 --> 00:23:45,170
Brandon!

179
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,770
I saw the king. He's got hundreds of people.

180
00:23:48,770 --> 00:23:52,060
How many times have I told you no climbing?

181
00:23:52,060 --> 00:23:55,150
But he's coming right now... down our road.

182
00:24:01,940 --> 00:24:04,320
I want you to promise me,

183
00:24:04,360 --> 00:24:06,420
no more climbing.

184
00:24:11,100 --> 00:24:12,460
I promise.

185
00:24:14,240 --> 00:24:17,130
- Do you know what? - What?

186
00:24:17,130 --> 00:24:20,600
You always look at your feet before you lie.

187
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:25,480
Run and find your father. Tell him the King is close.

188
00:25:10,110 --> 00:25:13,960
Where's Arya? Sansa, where's your sister?

189
00:25:26,270 --> 00:25:27,780
What are you doing with that on?

190
00:25:30,430 --> 00:25:31,570
Go on.

191
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:35,110
Move!

192
00:26:58,190 --> 00:26:59,420
Your Grace.

193
00:27:04,310 --> 00:27:05,980
You've got fat.

194
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:20,150
- Cat! - Your Grace.

195
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:26,130
Nine years... Why haven't I seen you?

196
00:27:26,130 --> 00:27:27,420
Where the hell have you been?

197
00:27:27,420 --> 00:27:29,530
Guarding the north for you, Your Grace.

198
00:27:29,530 --> 00:27:31,150
Winterfell is yours.

199
00:27:34,590 --> 00:27:37,470
- Where's the Imp? - Will you shut up?

200
00:27:37,730 --> 00:27:39,320
Who have we here?

201
00:27:40,710 --> 00:27:42,310
You must be Robb.

202
00:27:44,600 --> 00:27:47,020
My, you're a pretty one.

203
00:27:48,570 --> 00:27:50,260
Your name is?

204
00:27:50,710 --> 00:27:51,890
Arya.

205
00:27:52,590 --> 00:27:55,530
Oh, show us your muscles.

206
00:27:57,200 --> 00:27:58,980
You'll be a soldier.

207
00:28:01,810 --> 00:28:04,230
That's Jaime Lannister, the Queen's twin brother.

208
00:28:04,230 --> 00:28:06,280
Would you please shut up?

209
00:28:16,180 --> 00:28:17,400
My Queen.

210
00:28:18,150 --> 00:28:19,330
My Queen.

211
00:28:19,790 --> 00:28:22,150
Take me to your crypt. I want to pay my respects.

212
00:28:22,150 --> 00:28:24,360
We've been riding for a month, my love.

213
00:28:24,360 --> 00:28:26,470
Surely the dead can wait.

214
00:28:26,540 --> 00:28:27,610
Ned.

215
00:28:37,840 --> 00:28:39,340
Where's the Imp?

216
00:28:42,790 --> 00:28:44,460
Where is our brother?

217
00:28:44,560 --> 00:28:46,540
Go and find the little beast.

218
00:28:48,600 --> 00:28:50,210
Tell me about Jon Arryn.

219
00:28:51,550 --> 00:28:54,210
One minute he was fine and then...

220
00:28:55,020 --> 00:28:57,990
Burned right through him, whatever it was.

221
00:28:58,910 --> 00:29:00,440
I loved that man.

222
00:29:01,260 --> 00:29:02,680
We both did.

223
00:29:03,310 --> 00:29:05,550
He never had to teach you much, but me?

224
00:29:05,550 --> 00:29:07,340
You remember me at 16?

225
00:29:07,970 --> 00:29:08,930
All I wanted to do

226
00:29:08,930 --> 00:29:11,680
was crack skulls and fuck girls.

227
00:29:11,680 --> 00:29:14,460
- He showed me what was what. - Aye.

228
00:29:14,990 --> 00:29:18,170
Don't look at me like that. It's not his fault I didn't listen.

229
00:29:22,120 --> 00:29:23,860
I need you, Ned...

230
00:29:24,420 --> 00:29:25,660
down at King's Landing,

231
00:29:25,660 --> 00:29:28,250
not up here where you're no damn use to anybody.

232
00:29:29,810 --> 00:29:32,080
Lord Eddard Stark,

233
00:29:32,550 --> 00:29:35,080
I would name you the Hand of the King.

234
00:29:39,550 --> 00:29:41,230
I'm not worthy of the honor.

235
00:29:41,740 --> 00:29:43,420
I'm not trying to honor you.

236
00:29:43,420 --> 00:29:45,120
I'm trying to get you to run my kingdom

237
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:49,190
while I eat, drink and whore my way to an early grave.

238
00:29:49,190 --> 00:29:51,180
Damn it, Ned, stand up.

239
00:29:52,590 --> 00:29:54,480
You helped me win the Iron Throne,

240
00:29:54,490 --> 00:29:56,800
now help me keep the damn thing.

241
00:29:57,260 --> 00:30:00,000
We were meant to rule together.

242
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:04,120
If your sister had lived, we'd have been bound by blood.

243
00:30:04,610 --> 00:30:06,400
Well, it's not too late.

244
00:30:07,760 --> 00:30:09,930
I have a son, you have a daughter.

245
00:30:11,650 --> 00:30:13,330
We'll join our houses.

246
00:30:38,160 --> 00:30:41,410
It is true what they say about the northern girls.

247
00:30:49,440 --> 00:30:51,450
Did you hear the King's in Winterfell?

248
00:30:51,860 --> 00:30:53,820
I did hear something about that.

249
00:30:53,820 --> 00:30:55,980
And the Queen and her twin brother.

250
00:30:55,980 --> 00:30:59,000
They say that he is the most handsome man in the Seven Kingdoms.

251
00:30:59,010 --> 00:31:00,630
And the other brother?

252
00:31:01,070 --> 00:31:04,510
- The queen has two brothers? - There's the pretty one,

253
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:07,590
and there's the clever one.

254
00:31:08,580 --> 00:31:12,680
Mmm, I hear they call him the Imp.

255
00:31:12,940 --> 00:31:14,970
I hear he hates that nickname.

256
00:31:14,970 --> 00:31:17,900
Oh? I hear he's more than earned it.

257
00:31:18,030 --> 00:31:20,350
I hear he's a drunken little lecher,

258
00:31:20,350 --> 00:31:23,090
prone to all manner of perversions.

259
00:31:23,500 --> 00:31:25,300
Clever girl.

260
00:31:26,520 --> 00:31:28,830
We've been expecting you, Lord Tyrion.

261
00:31:29,530 --> 00:31:30,840
Have you?

262
00:31:31,200 --> 00:31:32,720
Oh! Already?

263
00:31:35,390 --> 00:31:37,600
The gods gave me one blessing.

264
00:31:43,060 --> 00:31:45,830
- Don't get up. - My lord.

265
00:31:45,830 --> 00:31:47,930
Should I explain to you the meaning of a closed door

266
00:31:47,930 --> 00:31:49,630
in a whorehouse, brother?

267
00:31:49,630 --> 00:31:51,700
You have much to teach me, no doubt,

268
00:31:51,700 --> 00:31:55,330
but our sister craves your attention.

269
00:31:55,870 --> 00:31:58,100
She has odd cravings, our sister.

270
00:31:58,100 --> 00:31:59,720
A family trait.

271
00:31:59,960 --> 00:32:02,590
Now the Starks are feasting us at sundown.

272
00:32:03,420 --> 00:32:05,070
Don't leave me alone with these people.

273
00:32:05,080 --> 00:32:07,670
I'm sorry, I've begun the feast a bit early.

274
00:32:07,670 --> 00:32:11,020
And this is the first of many courses.

275
00:32:11,400 --> 00:32:13,130
I thought you might say that.

276
00:32:13,380 --> 00:32:15,610
But since we're short on time...

277
00:32:16,050 --> 00:32:17,490
Come on, girls.

278
00:32:23,270 --> 00:32:24,830
See you at sundown.

279
00:32:25,190 --> 00:32:26,800
Close the door!

280
00:32:39,750 --> 00:32:42,760
Did you have to bury her in a place like this?

281
00:32:44,290 --> 00:32:46,480
She should be on a hill somewhere

282
00:32:46,480 --> 00:32:49,120
with the sun and the clouds above her.

283
00:32:49,120 --> 00:32:50,990
She was my sister.

284
00:32:51,620 --> 00:32:53,410
This is where she belongs.

285
00:32:54,030 --> 00:32:56,100
She belonged with me.

286
00:33:01,910 --> 00:33:05,150
In my dreams, I kill him every night.

287
00:33:06,660 --> 00:33:09,170
It's done, Your Grace.

288
00:33:09,660 --> 00:33:11,540
The Targaryens are gone.

289
00:33:14,130 --> 00:33:15,740
Not all of them.

290
00:33:26,980 --> 00:33:28,280
Daenerys!

291
00:33:32,460 --> 00:33:33,600
Daenerys.

292
00:33:34,060 --> 00:33:35,880
There's our bride-to-be.

293
00:33:37,030 --> 00:33:40,170
Look, a gift from Illyrio.

294
00:33:41,170 --> 00:33:42,360
Touch it.

295
00:33:42,900 --> 00:33:45,110
Go on, feel the fabric.

296
00:33:53,550 --> 00:33:55,590
Isn't he a gracious host?

297
00:33:58,490 --> 00:33:59,970
We've been his guests for over a year

298
00:33:59,970 --> 00:34:02,230
and he's never asked us for anything.

299
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:03,970
Illyrio's no fool.

300
00:34:04,210 --> 00:34:06,130
He knows I won't forget my friends

301
00:34:06,130 --> 00:34:08,100
when I come into my throne.

302
00:34:12,630 --> 00:34:14,440
You still slouch.

303
00:34:19,210 --> 00:34:20,910
Let them see.

304
00:34:24,060 --> 00:34:26,720
You have a woman's body now.

305
00:34:44,470 --> 00:34:46,620
I need you to be perfect today.

306
00:34:49,160 --> 00:34:50,770
Can you do that for me?

307
00:34:54,190 --> 00:34:56,590
You don't want to wake the dragon, do you?

308
00:34:58,770 --> 00:34:59,990
No.

309
00:35:06,970 --> 00:35:09,610
When they write the history of my reign, sweet sister,

310
00:35:09,610 --> 00:35:11,860
they will say it began today.

311
00:35:35,300 --> 00:35:36,990
It's too hot, my lady.

312
00:35:58,360 --> 00:35:59,600
Where is he?

313
00:36:00,170 --> 00:36:03,140
The Dothraki are not known for their punctuality.

314
00:36:16,650 --> 00:36:20,540
Athchomar chomakaan, Khal vezhven.

315
00:36:20,930 --> 00:36:23,250
May I present my honored guests?

316
00:36:23,300 --> 00:36:26,260
Viserys of House Targaryen,

317
00:36:26,260 --> 00:36:27,890
the third of his name,

318
00:36:27,890 --> 00:36:31,210
the rightful King of the Andals and the First Men,

319
00:36:31,260 --> 00:36:32,720
and his sister

320
00:36:32,730 --> 00:36:35,440
Daenerys of House Targaryen.

321
00:36:39,090 --> 00:36:41,040
Do you see how long his hair is?

322
00:36:41,570 --> 00:36:44,020
When Dothraki are defeated in combat,

323
00:36:44,190 --> 00:36:48,070
they cut off their braids so the whole world can see their shame.

324
00:36:48,070 --> 00:36:52,110
Khal Drogo has never been defeated.

325
00:36:53,120 --> 00:36:54,510
He's a savage, of course,

326
00:36:54,510 --> 00:36:57,140
but one of the finest killers alive.

327
00:36:58,800 --> 00:37:00,850
And you will be his queen.

328
00:37:01,350 --> 00:37:02,950
Come forward, my dear.

329
00:37:43,260 --> 00:37:44,500
Where is he going?!

330
00:37:44,500 --> 00:37:47,350
- The ceremony is over. - But he didn't say anything.

331
00:37:47,350 --> 00:37:50,050
- Did he like her? - Trust me, Your Grace,

332
00:37:50,050 --> 00:37:52,380
if he didn't like her, we'd know.

333
00:37:55,450 --> 00:37:57,090
It won't be long now.

334
00:37:57,750 --> 00:37:59,650
Soon you will cross the Narrow Sea

335
00:37:59,650 --> 00:38:01,960
and take back your father's throne.

336
00:38:02,730 --> 00:38:05,180
The people drink secret toasts

337
00:38:05,180 --> 00:38:06,720
to your health.

338
00:38:06,720 --> 00:38:09,330
They cry out for their true king.

339
00:38:12,760 --> 00:38:14,460
When will they be married?

340
00:38:14,680 --> 00:38:18,460
Soon. The Dothraki never stay still for long.

341
00:38:18,460 --> 00:38:20,950
Is it true they lie with their horses?

342
00:38:21,360 --> 00:38:23,660
I wouldn't ask Khal Drogo.

343
00:38:23,830 --> 00:38:25,690
Do you take me for a fool?

344
00:38:26,050 --> 00:38:27,850
I take you for a king.

345
00:38:27,910 --> 00:38:31,140
Kings lack the caution of common men.

346
00:38:31,140 --> 00:38:33,180
My apologies if I've given offense.

347
00:38:33,180 --> 00:38:35,720
I know how to play a man like Drogo.

348
00:38:35,720 --> 00:38:38,870
I give him a queen and he gives me an army.

349
00:38:39,510 --> 00:38:41,410
I don't want to be his queen.

350
00:38:46,450 --> 00:38:47,990
I want to go home.

351
00:38:48,630 --> 00:38:49,880
So do I.

352
00:38:51,180 --> 00:38:53,660
I want us both to go home,

353
00:38:53,660 --> 00:38:55,890
but they took it from us.

354
00:38:55,890 --> 00:38:57,630
So tell me, sweet sister,

355
00:38:57,790 --> 00:38:59,770
how do we go home?

356
00:39:02,130 --> 00:39:03,510
I don't know.

357
00:39:03,550 --> 00:39:06,250
We go home with an army.

358
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:10,560
With Khal Drogo's army.

359
00:39:11,110 --> 00:39:14,230
I would let his whole tribe fuck you...

360
00:39:14,360 --> 00:39:17,820
All 40,000 men and their horses too

361
00:39:17,820 --> 00:39:19,640
if that's what it took.

362
00:39:36,740 --> 00:39:38,940
Do you think Joffrey will like me?

363
00:39:39,420 --> 00:39:41,200
What if he thinks I'm ugly?

364
00:39:41,630 --> 00:39:45,500
Then he is the stupidest prince that ever lived.

365
00:39:47,570 --> 00:39:49,530
He's so handsome.

366
00:39:50,240 --> 00:39:53,050
When would we be married? Soon? Or do we have to wait?

367
00:39:53,050 --> 00:39:56,220
Hush now. Your father hasn't even said yes.

368
00:39:56,300 --> 00:39:58,100
Why would he say no?

369
00:39:58,150 --> 00:40:01,390
He'd be the second most powerful man in the kingdoms.

370
00:40:01,410 --> 00:40:03,290
He'd have to leave home.

371
00:40:04,420 --> 00:40:06,270
He'd have to leave me.

372
00:40:07,750 --> 00:40:09,480
And so would you.

373
00:40:10,010 --> 00:40:12,290
You left your home to come here.

374
00:40:12,510 --> 00:40:14,680
And I'd be queen someday.

375
00:40:16,200 --> 00:40:17,960
Please make father say yes!

376
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:19,920
- Sansa... - Please please!

377
00:40:19,920 --> 00:40:22,610
It's the only thing I ever wanted.

378
00:40:36,620 --> 00:40:39,030
Fill that up! Boys, Rodrik, come on.

379
00:40:39,030 --> 00:40:40,200
Come on!

380
00:40:59,690 --> 00:41:01,180
Is he dead yet?

381
00:41:06,240 --> 00:41:07,830
Uncle Benjen.

382
00:41:10,240 --> 00:41:11,620
You got bigger.

383
00:41:13,050 --> 00:41:16,910
Rode all day. Didn't want to leave you alone with the Lannisters.

384
00:41:17,720 --> 00:41:19,180
Why aren't you at the feast?

385
00:41:19,450 --> 00:41:21,700
Lady Stark thought it might insult the royal family

386
00:41:21,710 --> 00:41:23,730
to seat a bastard in their midst.

387
00:41:24,740 --> 00:41:26,830
Well, you're always welcome on the wall.

388
00:41:27,240 --> 00:41:29,400
No bastard was ever refused a seat there.

389
00:41:29,400 --> 00:41:31,170
So take me with you when you go back.

390
00:41:31,170 --> 00:41:33,840
- Jon... - Father will let me if you ask him.

391
00:41:33,840 --> 00:41:35,540
I know he will.

392
00:41:38,380 --> 00:41:40,490
The wall isn't going anywhere.

393
00:41:40,890 --> 00:41:42,230
I'm ready

394
00:41:42,230 --> 00:41:43,920
to swear your oath.

395
00:41:44,070 --> 00:41:46,470
You don't understand what you'd be giving up.

396
00:41:46,800 --> 00:41:48,390
We have no families.

397
00:41:48,870 --> 00:41:52,450
- None of us will ever father sons... - I don't care about that!

398
00:41:52,880 --> 00:41:56,240
You might, if you knew what it meant.

399
00:41:59,150 --> 00:42:00,980
I'd better get inside,

400
00:42:01,580 --> 00:42:03,950
rescue your father from his guests.

401
00:42:06,720 --> 00:42:08,230
We'll talk later.

402
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:19,400
Your uncle's in the Night's Watch.

403
00:42:22,570 --> 00:42:24,170
What are you doing back there?

404
00:42:25,110 --> 00:42:27,760
Preparing for a night with your family.

405
00:42:32,580 --> 00:42:34,550
I've always wanted to see the wall.

406
00:42:34,560 --> 00:42:36,260
You're Tyrion Lannister,

407
00:42:37,090 --> 00:42:38,450
the queen's brother?

408
00:42:38,450 --> 00:42:40,440
My greatest accomplishment.

409
00:42:41,300 --> 00:42:44,550
And you... you're Ned Stark's bastard, aren't you?

410
00:42:47,520 --> 00:42:49,890
Did I offend you? Sorry.

411
00:42:51,910 --> 00:42:53,800
You are the bastard though.

412
00:42:55,550 --> 00:42:57,840
Lord Eddard Stark is my father.

413
00:42:58,980 --> 00:43:01,600
And Lady Stark is not your mother,

414
00:43:01,710 --> 00:43:05,090
making you the bastard.

415
00:43:06,370 --> 00:43:08,750
Let me give you some advice, bastard.

416
00:43:10,110 --> 00:43:11,820
Never forget what you are.

417
00:43:11,950 --> 00:43:13,950
The rest of the world will not.

418
00:43:14,570 --> 00:43:16,360
Wear it like armor

419
00:43:16,850 --> 00:43:19,090
and it can never be used to hurt you.

420
00:43:20,920 --> 00:43:23,500
What the hell do you know about being a bastard?

421
00:43:25,910 --> 00:43:28,860
All dwarves are bastards in their father's eyes.

422
00:43:50,590 --> 00:43:54,790
You at a feast... It's like a bear in a trap.

423
00:43:56,360 --> 00:44:00,310
The boy I beheaded... Did you know him?

424
00:44:00,320 --> 00:44:01,570
Of course I did.

425
00:44:01,580 --> 00:44:02,960
Just a lad.

426
00:44:03,550 --> 00:44:05,470
And he was tough, Ned,

427
00:44:05,840 --> 00:44:07,400
a true ranger.

428
00:44:08,960 --> 00:44:10,730
He was talking madness.

429
00:44:11,840 --> 00:44:13,710
Said the walkers slaughtered his friends.

430
00:44:13,710 --> 00:44:15,920
The two he was with are still missing.

431
00:44:18,000 --> 00:44:21,310
Hmph. A wildling ambush.

432
00:44:21,970 --> 00:44:23,370
Maybe.

433
00:44:24,370 --> 00:44:26,790
Direwolves south of the wall,

434
00:44:26,960 --> 00:44:28,910
talk of the walkers,

435
00:44:29,290 --> 00:44:32,390
and my brother might be the next Hand of the King.

436
00:44:33,020 --> 00:44:34,870
Winter is coming.

437
00:44:36,630 --> 00:44:38,320
Winter is coming.

438
00:44:39,630 --> 00:44:42,740
- Uncle Benjen. - Robb boy.

439
00:44:42,740 --> 00:44:44,860
- How are you? - I'm good.

440
00:44:47,940 --> 00:44:50,680
Is this your first time in the north, Your Grace?

441
00:44:50,730 --> 00:44:53,580
Yes. Lovely country.

442
00:44:57,270 --> 00:45:00,890
I'm sure it's very grim after King's Landing.

443
00:45:01,820 --> 00:45:03,890
I remember how scared I was when Ned brought me

444
00:45:03,890 --> 00:45:06,160
up here for the first time.

445
00:45:08,350 --> 00:45:10,020
Hello, little dove.

446
00:45:11,110 --> 00:45:13,030
But you are a beauty.

447
00:45:13,470 --> 00:45:16,080
- How old are you? - 13, Your Grace.

448
00:45:16,080 --> 00:45:18,890
You're tall. Still growing?

449
00:45:18,890 --> 00:45:20,900
I think so, Your Grace.

450
00:45:21,200 --> 00:45:23,190
And have you bled yet?

451
00:45:27,650 --> 00:45:29,600
No, Your Grace.

452
00:45:30,760 --> 00:45:32,870
Your dress, did you make it?

453
00:45:34,100 --> 00:45:37,630
Such a talent. You must make something for me.

454
00:45:39,640 --> 00:45:42,290
I hear we might share a grandchild someday.

455
00:45:43,330 --> 00:45:44,780
I hear the same.

456
00:45:44,780 --> 00:45:47,030
Your daughter will do well in the Capital.

457
00:45:47,190 --> 00:45:50,380
Such a beauty shouldn't stay hidden up here forever.

458
00:46:07,280 --> 00:46:10,040
- Your pardon. - I hear we might be neighbors soon.

459
00:46:10,040 --> 00:46:11,780
- I hope it's true. - Yes,

460
00:46:11,780 --> 00:46:13,770
the king has honored me with his offer.

461
00:46:13,770 --> 00:46:14,850
I'm sure we'll have a tournament

462
00:46:14,850 --> 00:46:17,380
to celebrate your new title... if you accept.

463
00:46:17,550 --> 00:46:19,270
It would be good to have you on the field.

464
00:46:19,270 --> 00:46:21,410
The competition has become a bit stale.

465
00:46:21,740 --> 00:46:24,270
- I don't fight in tournaments. - No?

466
00:46:24,270 --> 00:46:26,300
Getting a little old for it?

467
00:46:27,670 --> 00:46:29,550
I don't fight in tournaments

468
00:46:29,760 --> 00:46:31,700
because when I fight a man for real

469
00:46:32,350 --> 00:46:34,420
I don't want him to know what I can do.

470
00:46:36,200 --> 00:46:37,890
Well said.

471
00:46:39,580 --> 00:46:41,030
Arya!

472
00:46:42,720 --> 00:46:44,360
It's not funny!

473
00:46:44,920 --> 00:46:46,650
She always does this.

474
00:46:47,410 --> 00:46:49,200
This was my favorite dress.

475
00:46:49,890 --> 00:46:52,490
She always does it and it's not funny!

476
00:46:52,640 --> 00:46:54,040
Time for bed.

477
00:47:05,330 --> 00:47:06,910
I'm a Northman.

478
00:47:08,720 --> 00:47:11,000
I belong here with you, not down south

479
00:47:11,000 --> 00:47:13,730
in that rats' nest they call a Capital.

480
00:47:14,340 --> 00:47:17,340
I won't let him take you.

481
00:47:18,590 --> 00:47:20,660
The king takes what he wants.

482
00:47:22,110 --> 00:47:23,700
That's why he's king.

483
00:47:24,650 --> 00:47:28,980
I'll say, "Listen, fat man."

484
00:47:29,620 --> 00:47:32,570
"You are not taking my husband anywhere.

485
00:47:33,020 --> 00:47:35,060
He belongs to me now."

486
00:47:38,520 --> 00:47:40,660
How did he get so fat?

487
00:47:40,740 --> 00:47:43,820
He only stops eating when it's time for a drink.

488
00:47:46,910 --> 00:47:48,980
It's Maester Luwin, my lord.

489
00:47:50,580 --> 00:47:51,920
Send him in.

490
00:47:54,840 --> 00:47:56,770
Pardon, my lord, my lady.

491
00:47:57,830 --> 00:47:59,490
A rider in the night...

492
00:47:59,910 --> 00:48:01,300
From your sister.

493
00:48:09,730 --> 00:48:12,790
- Stay. - This was sent from the Eyrie.

494
00:48:18,250 --> 00:48:20,060
What's she doing at the Eyrie?

495
00:48:20,770 --> 00:48:23,240
She hasn't been back there since her wedding.

496
00:48:31,750 --> 00:48:33,000
What news?

497
00:48:35,240 --> 00:48:37,170
She's fled the Capital.

498
00:48:40,190 --> 00:48:42,760
She says Jon Arryn was murdered.

499
00:48:43,530 --> 00:48:44,950
By the Lannisters.

500
00:48:44,950 --> 00:48:47,120
She says the king is in danger.

501
00:48:47,700 --> 00:48:49,590
She's fresh widowed, Cat.

502
00:48:50,130 --> 00:48:51,620
She doesn't know what she's saying.

503
00:48:51,620 --> 00:48:54,250
Lysa's head would be on a spike right now

504
00:48:54,250 --> 00:48:56,780
if the wrong people had found that letter.

505
00:48:57,300 --> 00:48:59,430
Do you think she would risk her life...

506
00:48:59,430 --> 00:49:01,370
her son's life...

507
00:49:01,370 --> 00:49:04,640
if she wasn't certain her husband was murdered?

508
00:49:11,800 --> 00:49:13,600
If this news is true

509
00:49:13,600 --> 00:49:16,680
and the Lannisters conspire against the Throne,

510
00:49:17,500 --> 00:49:19,940
who but you can protect the king?

511
00:49:19,950 --> 00:49:22,150
They murdered the last hand.

512
00:49:22,250 --> 00:49:24,520
Now you want Ned to take the job?

513
00:49:24,520 --> 00:49:26,440
The king rode for a month

514
00:49:26,440 --> 00:49:28,730
to ask for Lord Stark's help.

515
00:49:28,730 --> 00:49:31,030
He's the only one he trusts.

516
00:49:32,620 --> 00:49:35,370
You swore the king an oath, my lord.

517
00:49:35,560 --> 00:49:39,170
He's spent half his life fighting Robert's wars.

518
00:49:39,290 --> 00:49:40,960
He owes him nothing.

519
00:49:43,250 --> 00:49:46,270
Your father and brother rode south once

520
00:49:46,650 --> 00:49:48,750
on a king's demand.

521
00:49:51,040 --> 00:49:52,810
A different time.

522
00:49:54,460 --> 00:49:56,020
A different king.

523
00:50:57,950 --> 00:50:59,480
When do I meet with the Khal?

524
00:50:59,880 --> 00:51:01,650
We need to begin planning the invasion.

525
00:51:01,650 --> 00:51:04,110
If Khal Drogo has promised you a crown,

526
00:51:04,110 --> 00:51:06,100
- you shall have it. - When?

527
00:51:06,100 --> 00:51:08,800
When their omens favor war.

528
00:51:09,150 --> 00:51:11,760
I piss on Dothraki omens.

529
00:51:12,050 --> 00:51:14,980
I've waited 17 years to get my throne back.

530
00:52:14,340 --> 00:52:15,640
A Dothraki wedding

531
00:52:15,640 --> 00:52:19,200
without at least three deaths is considered a dull affair.

532
00:52:32,200 --> 00:52:34,210
Jadi, zhey Jorah Andahli!

533
00:52:34,270 --> 00:52:35,810
Khal vezhven.

534
00:52:41,740 --> 00:52:45,000
A small gift, for the new khaleesi...

535
00:52:45,660 --> 00:52:48,500
Songs and Histories from the Seven Kingdoms.

536
00:52:50,060 --> 00:52:51,540
Thank you, ser.

537
00:52:53,210 --> 00:52:55,440
Are you from my country?

538
00:52:55,510 --> 00:52:58,000
Ser Jorah Mormont of Bear Island.

539
00:52:58,200 --> 00:53:00,710
I served your father for many years.

540
00:53:01,080 --> 00:53:04,660
Gods be good, I hope to always serve the rightful king.

541
00:53:27,330 --> 00:53:29,620
Dragon's eggs, Daenerys,

542
00:53:29,980 --> 00:53:32,750
from the Shadow Lands beyond Asshai.

543
00:53:32,970 --> 00:53:35,620
The ages have turned them to stone,

544
00:53:35,620 --> 00:53:37,950
but they will always be beautiful.

545
00:53:40,130 --> 00:53:42,100
Thank you, magister.

546
00:54:50,350 --> 00:54:52,340
She's beautiful.

547
00:54:56,650 --> 00:54:58,960
Ser Jorah, I don't know how to say

548
00:54:58,960 --> 00:55:00,950
thank you in Dothraki.

549
00:55:00,980 --> 00:55:03,980
There is no word for thank you in Dothraki.

550
00:55:24,930 --> 00:55:26,380
Make him happy.

551
00:56:26,390 --> 00:56:27,620
No.

552
00:56:31,840 --> 00:56:33,710
Do you know the common tongue?

553
00:56:39,370 --> 00:56:40,680
No.

554
00:56:44,270 --> 00:56:46,920
Is "No" The only word that you know?

555
00:56:48,170 --> 00:56:49,400
No.

556
00:57:18,010 --> 00:57:19,530
Rough night, Imp?

557
00:57:19,730 --> 00:57:21,990
If I get through this without squirting

558
00:57:21,990 --> 00:57:24,900
from one end or the other, it'll be a miracle.

559
00:57:25,390 --> 00:57:27,000
I didn't pick you for a hunter.

560
00:57:27,000 --> 00:57:30,210
The greatest in the land... my spear never misses.

561
00:57:31,050 --> 00:57:33,210
It's not hunting if you pay for it.

562
00:57:42,010 --> 00:57:44,400
Are you as good with a spear as you used to be?

563
00:57:44,480 --> 00:57:47,050
No, but I'm still better than you.

564
00:57:49,780 --> 00:57:51,510
I know what I'm putting you through.

565
00:57:51,510 --> 00:57:53,180
Thank you for saying yes.

566
00:57:55,340 --> 00:57:57,410
I only ask you because I need you.

567
00:57:58,710 --> 00:58:00,280
You're a loyal friend.

568
00:58:00,750 --> 00:58:04,170
You hear me? A loyal friend.

569
00:58:04,370 --> 00:58:06,040
The last one I've got.

570
00:58:07,490 --> 00:58:10,160
- I hope I'll serve you well. - You will.

571
00:58:10,900 --> 00:58:13,900
And I'll make sure you don't look so fucking grim all the time.

572
00:58:15,510 --> 00:58:18,120
Come on, boys, let's go kill some boar!

573
00:58:28,020 --> 00:58:29,270
Come on, you.

574
00:59:45,790 --> 00:59:46,760
Stop!

575
00:59:46,760 --> 00:59:47,890
Stop.

576
00:59:53,540 --> 00:59:55,520
Are you completely mad?

577
00:59:56,020 --> 00:59:58,670
- He saw us. - It's all right, it's all right.

578
00:59:58,670 --> 01:00:00,520
- It's all right. - He saw us!

579
01:00:00,530 --> 01:00:02,580
I heard you the first time.

580
01:00:07,600 --> 01:00:09,710
Quite the little climber, aren't you?

581
01:00:10,490 --> 01:00:13,560
- How old are you, boy? - 10.

582
01:00:14,100 --> 01:00:15,600
10.

583
01:00:23,760 --> 01:00:25,480
The things I do for love.

